.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
int \fBgf_kexinit_parse\fP (const uint8_t *payload, size_t len, struct gf_kexinit *out);
Parse a KEXINIT payload (starting with the message number).  The slices point into PAYLOAD.  Every list must be a valid name\-list.
.TP
int \fBgf_kexinit_make\fP (uint8_t *buf, size_t cap, size_t *len, int server, int initial, const struct gf_kex_prefs *prefs);
Build our KEXINIT, message number included, with a fresh cookie. INITIAL is nonzero for the first key exchange of a connection, which adds the strict and extension markers.  Returns GF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED if PREFS names a value policy does not permit.
.TP
int \fBgf_kexinit_negotiate\fP (const struct gf_kexinit *client, const struct gf_kexinit *server, int initial, struct gf_algs *out);
Choose the algorithms from the client's and the server's KEXINIT. Returns GF_OK; GF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED when nothing is in common (or compression cannot be turned off); GF_ERR_PROTOCOL when the peer guessed (first_kex_follows) or, if INITIAL, lacks strict key exchange.
